INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_call_id","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{"duration_ms" => 1, "ok" => true, "tool" => "read"}, 20, :tool, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "[scratch/kit/contents/README.md: 283 lines, showing 1–283]\n1\t# JobyKit\n2\t\n3\tAn opinionated, agentic-first design-system kit for Phoenix + daisyUI apps.\n4\t\n5\tJobyKit gives your AI coding agents a structured, machine-readable inventory\n6\tof every UI component your app exposes — with prop signatures, daisyUI basis,\n7\trendered previews, and a stable contract — so design and prototype phases\n8\tdon't accumulate a hodgepodge of UI markup that's hard to reason about.\n9\t\n10\t## Why this exists\n11\t\n12\tMost Phoenix apps end up with a sprawl of inline Tailwind classes, ad-hoc\n13\tcomponent shapes, and undocumented variants. AI coding agents working on\n14\tthose apps have to grep through HEEx to discover what's available and often\n15\tjust write new markup from scratch — making the sprawl worse.\n16\t\n17\tJobyKit pushes the codebase in the opposite direction. Your app declares a\n18\t**manifest** of its components, and JobyKit serves them at two surfaces:\n19\t\n20\t* `/design` — a curated, kit-uniform page showing your **core wrappers**\n21\t  (one per daisyUI primitive), the daisyUI catalogue, the wrapper contract,\n22\t  and the build-order decision tree. Same shape across every JobyKit\n23\t  consumer.\n24\t\n25\t* `/custom-designs` — your app's **composites and domain components**,\n26\t  separated from the kit's curated inventory so the kit page stays clean.\n27\t\n28\t* `/design.json` — a **single combined JSON endpoint** that an agent can\n29\t  fetch to get every component, attr, slot, and source path without\n30\t  parsing rendered HEEx.\n31\t\n32\t## Install\n33\t\n34\t### Generate a new app from scratch\n35\t\n36\tThe project generator ships as its own package, `joby_kit_new`, the same\n37\tway `phx_new` is separate from `phoenix`. It has to run before a project\n38\texists, so it installs as a Mix archive:\n39\t\n40\t```sh\n41\tmix archive.install hex joby_kit_new\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tThen from anywhere:\n45\t\n46\t```sh\n47\tmix joby_kit.new my_app   # wraps `mix phx.new` with the kit's HTML layer baked in\n48\tcd my_app\n49\tmix ecto.setup            # creates the dev DB and runs migrations\n50\tmix phx.server\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\tVisit `http://localhost:4000/`. `/design`, `/custom-designs`, and\n54\t`/design.json` are wired automatically.\n55\t\n56\t### Add to an existing Phoenix app\n57\t\n58\tAdd `joby_kit` to your `deps`:\n59\t\n60\t```elixir\n61\tdef deps do\n62\t  [\n63\t    {:joby_kit, \"~> 0.1\"}\n64\t  ]\n65\tend\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tThen run one of:\n69\t\n70\t```sh\n71\t# Adds the manifest, previews, design pages, and patches AGENTS.md +\n72\t# assets/css/app.css + your layout's nav. Idempotent.\n73\tmix joby_kit.install\n74\t\n75\t# Same as install, plus replaces the default HomeLive at /, removes\n76\t# PageController/PageHTML. For a kit-flavored greenfield start.\n77\tmix joby_kit.bootstrap\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t> JobyKit ships function components built on `phoenix_live_view ~> 1.0` and\n81\t> assumes daisyUI is installed in your Tailwind config (the default for\n82\t> Phoenix 1.7+ apps generated with `mix phx.new`). Heroicons via the\n83\t> `heroicons` Tailwind plugin is also expected.\n84\t\n85\tAfter running `install` or `bootstrap`, restart `mix phx.server`, visit\n86\t`/design` and `/custom-designs`, and `curl /design.json` to see the\n87\tmanifest.\n88\t\n89\tThe rest of this README walks through the same steps manually for projects\n90\tthat prefer a hand-rolled wiring.\n91\t\n92\t### 1. Declare your manifest\n93\t\n94\t```elixir\n95\tdefmodule MyAppWeb.DesignManifest do\n96\t  use JobyKit.Manifest\n97\t\n98\t  alias MyAppWeb.{CoreComponents, DesignPreviews}\n99\t\n100\t  category :core,\n101\t    label: \"Core wrappers\",\n102\t    description: \"One wrapper per daisyUI primitive.\"\n103\t\n104\t  category :composite,\n105\t    label: \"Composites\",\n106\t    description: \"Multi-primitive patterns reused across domains.\"\n107\t\n108\t  category :domain,\n109\t    label: \"Domain composites\",\n110\t    description: \"Composites tied to a product area.\"\n111\t\n112\t  component CoreComponents, :button,\n113\t    category: :core,\n114\t    daisy_basis: \"btn\",\n115\t    summary: \"Standard text button.\",\n116\t    preview: &DesignPreviews.button_preview/1\n117\t\n118\t  component CoreComponents, :card,\n119\t    category: " <> ..., "chatcmpl-tool-9c5964497b05a905", ~U[2026-09-11 07:49:42.414764Z], "4c1a43b3-2ab6-4ed1-847f-e668f7148b95"]
