INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 91, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nFixing issues in the test files (undefined `view` in helper, nonexistent `assert_has`, sloppy assertion, LazyHTML API usage).\n\n\n\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      assert has_element?(view, \"#signup-error\")\n      assert render(view) =~ \"already on the launch list\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"1\")\n\n      document = LazyHTML.from_fragment(render(view))\n      assert length(LazyHTML.filter(document, \"#signups li\")) == 1\n    end", "old_string" => "      assert has_element?(view, \"#signup-error\")\n      assert render(view) =~ \"already on the launch list\"\n      assert render(view) =~ \"1\" <> \"\" and has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"1\")\n      assert [li] = LazyHTML.filter(LazyHTML.from_fragment(render(view)), \"#signups li\")\n      assert li\n    end", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-9d85e492af2a8c0c", "name" => "edit"}, %{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      items = LazyHTML.filter(LazyHTML.from_fragment(render(view)), \"#activity li\")\n      assert length(items) == 10\n      assert LazyHTML.text(items) =~ \"dev12@lumen.dev\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"12\")\n    end\n  end\n\n  # The LiveView test clock is virtual: a blocking receive with a timeout\n  # advances it, which is how the 5s tick is scheduled in every env.\n  defp advance_clock(view, ms, step \\\\ 500) do\n    for _ <- 1..div(ms, step) do\n      receive do\n        _msg -> :ok\n      after\n        step -> :ok\n      end\n    end\n\n    # round-trip so the tick message is guaranteed handled before asserting\n    render(view)\n  end\nend", "old_string" => "      items = LazyHTML.filter(LazyHTML.from_fragment(render(view)), \"#activity li\")\n      assert length(items) == 10\n      first = LazyHTML.inner_html(List.first(items))\n      assert first =~ \"dev12@lumen.dev\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"12\")\n    end\n  end\n\n  # The LiveView test clock is virtual: a blocking receive with a timeout\n  # advances it, which is how the 5s tick is scheduled in every env.\n  defp advance_clock(ms, step \\\\ 500) do\n    for _ <- 1..div(ms, step) do\n      receive do\n        _msg -> :ok\n      after\n        step -> :ok\n      end\n    end\n\n    # round-trip so the tick message is guaranteed handled before asserting\n    render_update_dummy(view)\n  end\n\n  defp render_update_dummy(view), do: Phoenix.LiveViewTest.render(view)\nend", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b59d94509f3c0093", "name" => "edit"}, %{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      advance_clock(view, 6_000)", "old_string" => "      advance_clock(6_000)", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b4db0cb9539f8ff7", "name" => "edit"}, %{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "    assert render(view) =~ \"Meet Lumen\"\n  end", "old_string" => "    assert_has(view, \"Meet Lumen\")\n  end", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/about_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-9ade490a26afb1cb", "name" => "edit"}], "Issues with my tests:\n1. `assert render(view) =~ \"1\" <> \"\" and has_element?...` — sloppy leftover. Should just fix it to `assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"1\")`.\n2. `advance_clock` takes `view` but view isn't passed — helper arity: advance_clock(6_000) references render_update_dummy(view) — view is an undefined variable inside the helper (it's defined at the call site, not inside the helper). Fix: pass view.\n3. about test's assert_has — does that come from a Hound-ish style? What Phoenix.LiveViewTest has is `has_element?`, and assert_has doesn't exist. Use assert render =~ or text of element. Fix: `assert render(view) =~ \"Meet Lumen\"`. Note: after render_click on navigate link — element(#main-nav a[href=\"/about\"])|>render_click() for a <.link navigate> link works (it's a push of a live redirect).\n\nWait, the about test \"navigates from home to about\": view is HomeLive; the click on navigate link → render_click returns the new page's html; view is updated. OK.\n\nAlso LazyHTML: is LazyHTML's API `LazyHTML.from_fragment` + `LazyHTML.filter(document, selector)` + `LazyHTML.inner_html`? What exists: LazyHTML.from_fragment/1, filter/2, text/2? I'm not confident about inner_html. LazyHTML functions: `LazyHTML.text/1`? Do the functions operate on the selection returned by filter? In Phoenix LiveView docs LazyHTML: `document |> LazyHTML.from_fragment() |> LazyHTML.filter(\"p\") |> LazyHTML.at(0) |> LazyHTML.text()`. I think text/1 exists on a selection. Rewrite the duplicate test more simply: count with filter → `length(LazyHTML.filter(doc, \"#signups li\")) == 1`. For the text of the first activity item: does `LazyHTML.text(...)` return the text of the first element? The function operates on the selection, and text/1 returns the text of the first match. For now let's use the documented functions: LazyHTML.filter returns a selection; LazyHTML.at(selection, 0); LazyHTML.text(selection) → the text of the first node. Rewrite the tests accordingly, avoiding inner_html.\n\nAnother concern regarding the activity-cap test: 12 signups each → 12 activity entries, keep 10. Good.\n\nAnother potential issue: `form(\"#signup-form\", %{\"email\" => ...})` — form/3 fills in inputs with values keyed by name... `form(view, selector, params)` where params is a map of field values keyed by name... Actually, the 3rd argument of form/3 is `value` — is it a map of `%{\"field-name\" => value}`, or form-wide params? `form(view, \"#signup-form\", %{\"email\" => \"x\"})` — keys are input names (no nesting needed since there's no `as:`). OK.\n\nFix both test files now.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:07:07.631850Z], "1d795212-4cfe-4157-941f-6fbd0410a16f"]
