INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 103, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nModule attribute inside the extracted template — bind it in function code instead.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "  def app(assigns) do\n    nav_links = @nav_links\n\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div class=\"flex min-h-dvh flex-col bg-base-100\">\n      <div class=\"sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-base-300 bg-base-100/90 backdrop-blur\">\n        <div class=\"mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6\">\n          <CompositeComponents.app_nav\n            id=\"main-nav\"\n            active={@active_nav}\n            brand=\"Lumen\"\n            links={nav_links}\n          >", "old_string" => "  def app(assigns) do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <div class=\"flex min-h-dvh flex-col bg-base-100\">\n      <div class=\"sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-base-300 bg-base-100/90 backdrop-blur\">\n        <div class=\"mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6\">\n          <CompositeComponents.app_nav\n            id=\"main-nav\"\n            active={@active_nav}\n            brand=\"Lumen\"\n            links={@nav_links}\n          >", "path" => "benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/components/layouts.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-864889186afb23d2", "name" => "edit"}], "Compilation passes — but @nav_links is never used: module attributes are not automatically available inside HEEx templates! The `links={@nav_links}` inside the `app/1` template — module attributes should be accessible inside templates (templates get compiled into functions of the module). But the warning says \"set but never used,\" and my template references @nav_links... hmm, actually inside HEEx you can use module attributes. This warning suggests that the template did not pick it up — is it because I embedded `embed_templates \"layouts/*\"`? No... wait — my template references `links={@nav_links}` inside the `~H` sigil in layouts.ex. Module attributes do work inside function bodies. But... the warning came from the compiled module — maybe the assignment is being compiled in a different way. Actually, inside HEEx sigils within function definitions, module attributes should work fine. Why the \"never used\" warning?\n\nAh, I see — the `~H\"\"\"...\"\"\"` sigil is expanded at compile time by the Phoenix.Component.sigil_H/2 macro, and `@nav_links` inside there refers to Module.put_attribute at the expansion site — it should count as a use... but the compiler warning might be a false positive? No, actually — this is a known caveat: module attributes inside a `~H` sigil in a template do work and get interpolated at compile time (Phoenix compiles the sigil into code within the same module). For example, `@themes` in core_components works inside a `~H` (theme_toggle uses @themes assigned via assign() — hmm, that's different: they do `assigns = assign(assigns, :themes, @themes)` outside the sigil, and @themes is referenced in regular code).\n\nWait, inside NavComponent.simple_nav: `@default_links` is only used as a regular function default. And in the original layouts.ex template — @nav_links wasn't used (links were hardcoded via simple_nav's defaults).\n\nThe real question: does `@nav_links` inside `~H\"\"\"...\"\"\"` compile to a module attribute read? Phoenix.LiveView.HTMLAlgebra / sigil_H compiles attribute expressions: `links={@nav_links}` → the expression `@nav_links` is extracted and compiled as regular Elixir within the same module/function — should count as a use... but the warning says never used. So maybe it's resolved in a different form inside the sigil.\n\nHmm — but then does the link even render? If @nav_links resolves to a value at compile time, the warning shouldn't appear. The compiler's \"set but never used\" analysis is based on tracked get_attribute calls. Reads from inside macro expansion (sigil_H) do register as uses (they go through Module.get_attribute at expansion time inside the same module, and they do get tracked). Does Phoenix live compiler track template attribute uses? Actually, the live compiler moves compiled templates to a separate context/module chunk for optimization? The `phoenix_live_view` compiler extracts compiled template bodies to a separate module (LV 1.0's \"live dump / extraction to external module\" optimization!). That's the cause: compiled HEEx bodies get extracted to an \"external module\" in a post-processing step — reads of module attributes in there may not count as uses of layouts' attributes, and worse — reads of @nav_links in the extracted context could fail (undefined attribute error at runtime? Or maybe the extraction snapshots attributes...).\n\nGiven the uncertainty: the safest thing is to not use a module attribute inside the template: compute links with a regular private function `nav_links()` and use `links={nav_links()}`. Function calls are extracted fine (they get captured). Let me change it: `defp nav_links, do: [...]` and call it. Hmm — is calling a private function from inside extracted template code supported? It is — templates compile to functions that can call private functions in the same module; the extraction handles the module's functions.\n\nActually, an even simpler and definitely safe approach: bind the module attribute in regular code, before the sigil:\n```elixir\ndef app(assigns) do\n  nav_links = BenchappWeb.Layouts.nav_links?? \n```\nCan't reference yourself before definition; but the" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:08:07.906977Z], "efab4934-5662-4e80-962e-40e05a12e08f"]
