INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 107, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nLet me see the full failure messages.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"command" => "cd /Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp && mix test test/benchapp_web/live/about_live_test.exs:18 2>&1 | sed -n '1,60p'", "timeout_ms" => 60000}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-a3618afdc1c2e4d6", "name" => "bash"}], "Progress: 14 tests, 3 failures (the output was truncated so I only saw 2 failures. The third one is probably the about nav click or countdown). Failures:\n\n1) about \"navigates from home to about via the nav\": render_click on the nav link — stacktrace at live_view_test call/2 — the error text was truncated. Possibly clicked but got \"clicked element with phx-click but expected...\" — does a `navigate` link have phx-navigate? Or did an actual error occur during navigation — need full error.\n\n2) Duplicate signups: `LazyHTML.filter(document, \"#signups li\")` → 0 nodes! And items 0 nodes in the activity test. Meaning the stream items aren't in the rendered HTML?? But test 1 \"valid email is added\" passed? It used has_element?(view, \"#signups li\", ...) — did that pass? Of the visible failures, 3) is the activity cap count 0 — the stream items aren't appearing in render(view)'s HTML.\n\nImportant insight: `render(view)` returns the full rendered HTML — but do stream items show up in the rendered result? For streams, render/1 returns the diff-based \"full\" HTML, and it should include stream-inserted children. Hmm, but filter found 0 nodes. Maybe the rendered HTML uses comments (phx-stream comments) around stream items — no, if that were the case the li itself should still match.\n\nWait — the reason stream inserts didn't happen at all could be that my `stream(:signups, ...)` uses `at: 0` with `id: :id` as default. If the entry has an :id key → no problem. If insert was failing, render_submit should error out. Hmm.\n\nOr — LazyHTML.filter with a document from from_fragment — maybe a different usage is needed: `LazyHTML.filter(document, selector)` where document is a LazyHTML struct. My usage looks correct. 0 nodes suggests the li items truly don't exist in that fragment.\n\nLet's debug: run the duplicate test standalone with IO.inspect of the html. No, first let's see the full output of the first 2 failures (which are truncated). Rerun with more visible output.\n\nHypothesis on why li is missing: the \"valid email is added\" test probably passed with has_element? (it wasn't listed as a failure). has_element? uses the same rendered HTML. So in that test the li exists. In the duplicate test: after the second submit with the same email... the error path assigns form but doesn't touch the stream. HTML should still contain the li from the first submit. However... second submit %{\"email\" => \"dev@lumen.dev\"} → error path → OK, li remains. But LazyHTML sees 0. Difference: has_element? vs LazyHTML.from_fragment(render(view)). Both use render... unless has_element? actually failed earlier?? The output is truncated — the first failure might have been the valid signup test! Total failures are 3, and #2 (duplicate) #3 (activity cap) are visible, and #1 is partially visible (the about nav is failure... no, the code: |> render_click() snippet is failure... labeled \"code: |> render_click()\" and stacktrace is about_live_test:22 — is that failure \"2)\"? No — the block above is failure 1) (the truncated top). The failure list: 1) about nav click (render_click error), 2) duplicate LazyHTML, 3) activity cap LazyHTML. The \"valid email added\" test passed → stream items do render. So LazyHTML.filter returning 0 nodes — maybe the document fragment doesn't match \"#signups li\" because render(view)'s full HTML contains the entire LV wrapper and phx tracking comments. Even so, querySelector on a fragment should normally work... but the ul in the fragment — hmm! phx-update=\"stream\" renders children wrapped in comments: `<!-- <li ...> -->`? No wait — in LiveView streams, the initial rendering of a stream section uses `phx-stream` comment markers around the children only for dynamic parts. The rendered HTML of inserted stream items is a diff that patches the client, but render(view) returns the server-side full render and... hmm, in render/1's full HTML, stream children are rendered as-is.\n\nHowever — `debug_heex_annotations: true` in DEV config! No wait, debug_heex_annotations is dev-only; the test env config has enable_expensive_runtime_checks but not heex annotations.\n\nWait a s" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:09:42.545535Z], "28496bce-8abd-4970-badd-acb8ffa8fc27"]
