INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 118, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", [%{"arguments" => %{"command" => "cd /Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp && MIX_ENV=test mix run -e '\ndoc = LazyHTML.from_fragment(\"<ul><li>a</li><li>b</li></ul>\")\nIO.inspect(LazyHTML.filter(doc, \"li\"), label: \"simple\")\nh = ~s(<div id=\"wrap\"><ul id=\"signups\" phx-update=\"stream\"><li id=\"signups-a@b.com\" data-phx-stream=\"0\">x</li></ul></div>)\nd2 = LazyHTML.from_fragment(h)\nIO.inspect(LazyHTML.filter(d2, \"#signups li\"), label: \"id\")\n' 2>&1 | tail -10", "timeout_ms" => 60000}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-81aeced3a413f730", "name" => "bash"}], "`filter(%LazyHTML{}, selector)` is the correct signature. However, even with an html that contains li, `filter(doc, \"li\")` returned 0 nodes. Could it be that from_fragment is failing on the phx tracking comment `<!-- ... -->` that wraps `<div phx-feedback-for...>`? Or does the render HTML contain a `<!DOCTYPE`? Or is there a NIF parsing error on attributes like `<span phx-r=\"\"`...? The 307 line example uses from_fragment together with filter — no problem. Could it be that the problem is that the render(view) string starts with the dynamic marker `<!-- <div ...> -->`? The section dump shows that html is actual markup.\n\nWait a moment — the problem might be this: my html fragment contains an unclosed or weird structure, and NIF parsing is broken from an early stage (e.g., `<html>` inside a `<textarea>`... no, that's not it). Even the plain \"li\" gets 0 hits. Let me test the minimal case: from_fragment(\"<ul><li>x</li></ul>\") |> filter(\"li\"). Quick check with `mix run -e`.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:10:55.114471Z], "c5f20947-aebe-4ef5-b15f-6c6739920e0b"]
