INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 130, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\n`all/1` isn't available in LV 1.2 — I'll count via stream id markers in the rendered HTML.\n\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      assert has_element?(view, \"#signup-error\")\n      assert render(view) =~ \"already on the launch list\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"1\")\n\n      assert count_id_prefix(render(view), \"signups-\") == 1\n    end", "old_string" => "      assert has_element?(view, \"#signup-error\")\n      assert render(view) =~ \"already on the launch list\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"1\")\n\n      assert length(element(view, \"#signups li\") |> all()) == 1\n    end", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-84706f4703ad3019", "name" => "edit"}, %{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "      html = render(view)\n      assert count_id_prefix(html, \"activity-\") == 10\n      # newest first: the latest signup's entry appears before the previous one\n      assert :binary.match(html, \"dev12@lumen.dev\") < :binary.match(html, \"dev11@lumen.dev\")\n      # the two oldest entries were trimmed\n      refute html =~ \"dev2@lumen.dev joined\"\n      assert html =~ \"dev3@lumen.dev joined\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"12\")\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp count_id_prefix(html, prefix) do\n    case :binary.matches(html, ~s|id=\"\#{\"\#{prefix}\"}|) do\n      matches when is_list(matches) -> length(matches)\n    end\n  end", "old_string" => "      items = element(view, \"#activity li\") |> all()\n      assert length(items) == 10\n      assert hd(items) =~ \"dev12@lumen.dev\"\n      assert has_element?(view, \"#stat-signups\", \"12\")\n    end\n  end", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/home_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-883d359ad3d7d1d2", "name" => "edit"}], "all/1 is not exported (in LV 1.2's LiveViewTest, all/1 is deprecated/removed). Alternative counting methods that don't use LazyHTML:\n- `element(view, \"#activity li\") |> has_element?` only verifies existence.\n- Count via render + binary counting: count the occurrences of `data-phx-stream=\"` within #activity? Simple approach: count occurrences of the substring `id=\"activity_` within render(view)! Since the stream's child element ids are \"activity_<seq>\", counting them yields the li count. Similarly for signups, it's `id=\"signups_`.\n\nLet's verify the actual DOM ids: in the earlier dump it showed `<li id=\"signups-dev@lumen.dev\" ... data-phx-stream=\"0\">`. So li ids = \"signups-<key>\" (with hyphen!). For activity: \"activity-<seq>\". Count occurrences of the string `id=\"activity-` with something like binary matches. Use:\n\n```elixir\ndefp count_matches(view, prefix) do\n  html = render(view)\n  :binary.match(html, prefix, scope: :all) |> elem(1) |> length()\nend\n```\nScope :all returns a list of matches.\n\nDuplicate test: count `id=\"signups-` == 1. Cap test: count `id=\"activity-` == 10; latest-first: the first occurrence of \"activity-\" contains dev12 — easier: index of \"dev12@lumen.dev\" < index of \"dev11@lumen.dev\" within the html (newer ones appear earlier). Also assert that \"dev2@\" doesn't exist (trimmed) — only 10 out of 12 are retained (dev1, dev2 are deleted). The ordering is dev12 first... entries dev3..dev12 are retained. Assert html doesn't contain \"dev2@lumen.dev joined\" but does contain \"dev3@lumen.dev joined\".\n\nThe text of the first li: use `element(view, \"#activity li\") |> text()`? text/1 exists in LV 1.2 (element|>text returns the first match). Try text: does assert text(element(view, \"#activity li\")) =~ \"dev12\" — does element |> text() exist? I recall that `text/1` was deprecated in 0.18... maybe it was removed in 1.2? Safer to use: index comparison against the render html.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:12:20.097061Z], "cad8bea9-871b-4a51-862a-5fc92b071e57"]
