INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 136, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nOne failure left: after a `navigate` click the old view pid is gone — assert on the HTML returned by `render_click`.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "  test \"navigates from home to about via the nav\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n\n    html =\n      view\n      |> element(~S{#main-nav ul.menu-horizontal a[href=\"/about\"]})\n      |> render_click()\n\n    assert html =~ \"Meet Lumen\"\n  end", "old_string" => "  test \"navigates from home to about via the nav\", %{conn: conn} do\n    {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, ~p\"/\")\n\n    view\n    |> element(~S{#main-nav ul.menu-horizontal a[href=\"/about\"]})\n    |> render_click()\n\n    assert render(view) =~ \"Meet Lumen\"\n  end", "path" => "benchapp/test/benchapp_web/live/about_live_test.exs"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-8231c0e2a1a22cc2", "name" => "edit"}], "13/14 green. The about-nav transition test: after clicking a `navigate` link, the original LiveView (view) died — because navigating via push/redirect tears down the old view and spins up a new one, so `render(view)` on the old pid fails. In LiveViewTest, when you click a navigate link with element().render_click(), the view struct returned by render_click gets updated — but the *local variable* `view` stays stale. Does the test framework auto-replace it? On live_redirect, `render_click` returns the new HTML. To continue, use the updated view: `view = element(view, ...) |> render_click() |> elem?` Actually, in LVTest, for a live redirect via a link with data-phx-link=\"redirect\", after render_click the client proxy automatically switches to the new view — and the docs say to reassign: `html = render_click(link)`, and then does `view` still point to the client that hosts the new view? The error says the process is dead. The pattern that works:\n\n```elixir\n{:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, \"/\")\nview = element(view, selector) |> render_click() ... \n```\nrender_click returns HTML, not a view. Phoenix docs about live redirects in tests: \"When testing live_redirect, first render the page, then click the link with render_click, and then the test can assert on the rendered contents — the proxy reuses the same client\". But here the LV pid died because a new LiveView was spun up over the same websocket; the client proxy should rebind…\n\nHmm, maybe the issue is this: the data-phx-link-state=\"push\" link is a live_patch?? `navigate` link → live_redirect (state push). The client proxy handles the \"redirect\" event and joins the new LV — LiveViewTest supports this automatically (\"live_redirect is followed automatically\"). The error occurred on the `render(view)` after render_click succeeded. \"no process\" — the proxy is still pointing at the dead pid. Maybe the new view's join happens asynchronously. Do we need `render(view)`? Actually the returned HTML of render_click already contains the new page (\"Meet Lumen\"). Simplest is: assert against the returned html:\n\n```elixir\nhtml = element(view, ...) |> render_click()\nassert html =~ \"Meet Lumen\"\nassert has_element?(view, ~S{#main-nav a[href=\"/about\"][aria-current=\"page\"]})  # maybe the proxy is fine by this point? \n```\nhas_element? also calls the proxy. Stick to html-only assertions. Fix the test: capture html from render_click, and assert against it.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:12:58.903367Z], "da0201ee-e902-40b3-9dc0-edbcc9b36162"]
