INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 142, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", [%{"arguments" => %{"command" => "cd /Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp && grep -n \"def follow_redirect\\|def follow_redirect!\" deps/phoenix_live_view/lib/phoenix_live_view/test/live_view_test.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-a3679f91a37ce3ea", "name" => "bash"}], "render_click returns `{:error, {:live_redirect, %{to: \"/about\"}}}` — in LiveViewTest, for a live redirect, the standard pattern is as follows:\n\n```elixir\nassert {:error, {:live_redirect, %{to: \"/about\"}}} = render_click(link)\n```\n\nAfter that, continue the flow with follow_redirect(view, ...) — `follow_redirect!(view)` returns {:ok, new_view, html}. Use the following:\n\n```elixir\n{:error, {:live_redirect, %{to: \"/about\"}}} = view |> element(sel) |> render_click()\n{:ok, view2, html} = follow_redirect(view)  # in newer versions, follow_redirect/2\nassert html =~ \"Meet Lumen\"\nassert has_element?(view2, ~S{#main-nav a[href=\"/about\"][aria-current=\"page\"]})\n```\nDoes follow_redirect/1 exist in 1.2? Phoenix.LiveViewTest.follow_redirect/2 (view, to) is legacy; follow_redirect/1? There's also `follow_redirect(conn, view)`? In the LV docs: `follow_redirect(view)`? Hmm — Phoenix.LiveViewTest.follow_redirect(conn, path)… In 1.x: `follow_redirect(view)` and `follow_redirect!(view)` — deprecated in favor of…? Let me check the exports of live_view_test.ex.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:13:25.997476Z], "874c49d3-8617-4a63-8c3d-586acbe92d44"]
