INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 196, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nThe menu didn't open. Inspecting the button's phx-click payload.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"action" => "evaluate", "expression" => "(() => { const b = document.querySelector(\"#nav-toggle\"); return {phxClick: b.getAttribute(\"phx-click\"), liveConnected: !!document.querySelector(\"[phx-session]\")}; })()"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-b3401878362ec719", "name" => "preview"}], "The menu still has hidden:true after the click! JS.toggle didn't work. Why? The click occurred at (357,26) on #nav-toggle. JS.toggle(to: \"#mobile-menu\") — this JS command is set as the phx-click attribute. On click, LiveView JS should execute. But hidden remained true.\n\nPossible causes:\n1. The click happened before the LV socket was connected/reconnected? The page should be connected (countdown is updating → connected).\n2. JS.toggle default: toggle the hidden attribute — but if the element was initially `hidden`... JS.toggle checks the current state via the `hidden` attribute — should remove it. Hmm.\n\nWait — maybe it's the click event itself: the <button> inside the actions div of the nav — clicking at (357,26) hit nav-toggle. Actually there could be 2 elements matching #nav-toggle? No — preview is one instance (the preview page isn't here).\n\nLet me check: does phx-click contain a serialized JS command? Check the attribute value in the browser and manually dispatch/verify. Or, LiveView might need a `phx-hook`/JS binding: `phx-click` accompanied by JS works natively on connected clients (JS commands are JSON-encoded in the attribute). Let me examine the attribute.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:16:10.384361Z], "bf37f7bd-3fdc-4697-83dd-c8a8879a76dc"]
