INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8) [%{}, 198, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", [%{"arguments" => %{"action" => "evaluate", "expression" => "(() => { const b = document.querySelector(\"#nav-toggle\"); b.click(); const m = document.querySelector(\"#mobile-menu\"); const sess = !!document.querySelector(\"[data-phx-session]\"); return {hidden: m.hidden, phxSession: sess}; })()"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-8d8a2bb74231d005", "name" => "preview"}], "phx-click has the correct JS command JSON. But liveConnected: false — there's no [phx-session] element?? The countdown updated live earlier… wait, is the countdown updating? It showed 84 vs the earlier 95 — yes, it's live. So the socket is connected — but the `[phx-session]` selector is wrong: the wrapper div's attribute is `data-phx-session`, not `phx-session`. So liveConnected being false is an artifact of my selector.\n\nThe real problem: JS.toggle didn't execute on click. Hmm — actually maybe it did execute and… got hidden again? The click occurred at (357,26)… after the click I ran an evaluate that read hidden → true. Did the click toggle the hidden attribute and then something re-rendered? Does a countdown tick every 5 seconds re-render the entire layout?? The layout is mostly STATIC — app_nav is inside Layouts.app, rendered by the page LiveView's render. A countdown tick only re-renders the dynamic parts of HomeLive's template. But Layouts.app is rendered inside HomeLive.render — is the layout inside the same template? No: `<Layouts.app flash={@flash} active_nav=\"home\">` is the outer wrapper of HomeLive's template. When a tick changes assigns, does the layout re-render? The layout component's static parts are cached, but the `hidden` attribute on #mobile-menu is a literal static attribute within app_nav — a re-render should send diffs only for dynamic parts; the static hidden attribute doesn't change… However, when an entire static chunk re-renders (e.g., a stream patch), could the browser DOM node be replaced, losing the client-side toggled attribute? LiveView patches in place; static content isn't resent. But: my JS.toggle toggles the `hidden` attribute (setAttribute/removeAttribute) — if the DOM node itself isn't replaced, the attribute change persists. The entire menu div is static within the LV static chunk, so it shouldn't be touched.\n\nOr — maybe the click didn't execute the JS command because the element is inside a STATIC-rendered region… phx-click JS works regardless of that.\n\nWait — the click at (357,26) hit the BUTTON, but did preview actually dispatch a trusted click to the element? It reported click coordinates. LV should have processed it.\n\nHmm, possibility of a double-toggle?: the button click toggles open, and then the click also bubbles to some other… No.\n\nLet me test directly: dispatch the toggle from the console: evaluate `document.querySelector(\"#nav-toggle\").click()` and then check hidden. Also verify whether a countdown tick is replacing the nav's DOM: compare before/after. Actually the easiest is: manually click and immediately check. If still hidden, then the JS command isn't wired: maybe LiveSocket isn't connected!! Verify with the correct selector [data-phx-session]. If the socket is disconnected, phx-click does nothing — but the countdown is updating… it was updating (95→84). So the socket is connected.\n\nActually wait — did the menu toggle, and did the subsequent evaluate run after the click… the response shows hidden:true. Anyway, let me re-click and re-check.\n", ~U[2026-09-11 08:16:37.211253Z], "1697f135-3a97-4655-b421-ce4445bcc698"]
