INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 206, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nNo JS errors — let me read the client's `execToggle` implementation to find what's happening.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"command" => "cd /Users/jody/dgx-spark-model-bench/results/2026-09-10-baseline/work/qwen38-flash-next-nvfp4/benchapp && grep -n \"execToggle\\|toggleAttribute\\|toggleClass\" deps/phoenix_live_view/priv/static/phoenix_live_view.cjs.js | head -10"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-87194560fb2815c0", "name" => "bash"}], "No errors, but the menu isn't toggling at all. JS.dispatch worked, but JS.toggle isn't firing.\n\nHmm... let me reconsider: did JS.dispatch really work? The theme changed to dark. theme_toggle uses `JS.dispatch(\"phx:set-theme\")` — the root script listens for `phx:set-theme` on window and reads e.target.dataset.phxTheme → sets localStorage + data-theme. It worked → so the phx-click handler executed.\n\nSo then, why isn't toggle executing? ... Ah. It's gotta be the `static` chunk issue in LiveView 1.2! In LV 1.x, for phx-click elements inside a **static** (no-diff) region of a template — clicks are handled, yes, they're handled, via global delegation. Hmm.\n\nBut, another thought: the nav is rendered inside a component (`app_nav`), and the click on the button inside the component... same thing, no problem.\n\nLet me check what LiveView's exec is expecting as the toggle argument: serialized `[[\"toggle\",{\"to\":\"#mobile-menu\"}]]`. Inside live_view.js: the `push` and `applyReadonly` operations are... \"toggle\" case: `execToggle(el, signature, options)` — uses `options.attr` ?? default is \"hidden\". It's calling `hideEl/showEl` with `transition` and `time`... if no transition and no display: sets the attribute directly: `toggleAttribute`. Should work!\n\nCould it be... the app.js bundle is old, or doesn't match the LV server version?! Let me check the browser's LV JS version and the server version. assets/js/app.js imports LiveSocket from \"phoenix_live_view\" (the npm package under assets/node_modules? or from vendor). The generated app bundles LV's npm JS — if the esbuild watcher isn't running, or built an old one... but the socket is connected and countdown is running too (that's LV's JS!) and JS.dispatch works too. So the JS is normal.\n\nDifference between toggle and dispatch execution... in JS.exec (client), each op: `[op, args]` → looks up `LiveViewJS[command]`... `dispatch` and `toggle` are both methods. Hmm.\n\nWait — let me actually check the serialization result: for JS.toggle(to:) — the server encoded `[[\"toggle\",{\"to\":\"#mobile-menu\"}]]`. Client's execJS: `execFns.push(() => execJSCmd(el, cmd, ...))` and `switch(cmd)`: \"push\": ...; case \"toggle\": `execToggle(targetEl, signature, args)` where targetEl = querySelector(args.to). But the client's toggle implementation: `if (args.display) { ... } else { toggleDefault }` uses `options.attr || \"hidden\"`; calls `el.hasAttribute(attr) ? removeAttribute : setAttribute`?\n\nHonestly, it should work. Let me test another JS op via console to see whether it's exec itself: dispatch a custom event through another phx-click element...\n\nHmm — wait, another possibility: LiveView's delegated click handler resolves which LV/element handles the event, by walking up to `[phx-view|data-phx-view]`... in LV1.2, the handler checks `disableAnyForm`, then... it might require an `ownerView` found via `el.closest(\"[data-phx-session]\")`. The nav is inside the wrapper. Yes, it is inside (data-phx-session on the root div under body).\n\nOK, enough theorizing — a decisive experiment: call the client's exec via a known-good pattern: add another element? Too slow. Alternative pragmatic fix: swap JS.toggle for a colocated hook or a JS class toggle: `JS.toggle_class(\"hidden\", to: \"#mobile-menu\")`? toggle_class is also JS. If the class-based toggle works, I'll switch to that (my own `hidden` class, not the attribute). Test in browser: manually evaluate `document.querySelector(\"#mobile-menu\").classList.toggle(\"hidden\")` — that'll obviously work but doesn't prove phx wiring.\n\nDecisive test for exec: theme toggle's dispatch worked via delegated handler... so delegation works. Which means toggle-specifically: maybe my selector \"#mobile-menu\" — wait: the client's `execToggle` first looks at `el = querySelector` relative to the clicked element? `args.to` is an absolute selector → global. No problem.\n\nLet me look at the actual JS source of execToggle in the installed assets — check the client code in deps/phoenix_live_view/priv/static/phoenix_live_view.cjs.js to see whether the default for \"toggle\" behaves differently: maybe by defaul" <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:18:24.846480Z], "1f5238d2-6226-4842-9edf-540bb5ec90df"]
