INSERT INTO "messages" ("meta","seq","role","session_id","content","tool_calls","reasoning","inserted_at","id") VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9) [%{}, 218, :assistant, "4e0d427e-222d-494e-94c1-e4bae425157b", "\n\nJS.toggle is silently failing in the client even on a fresh load (dispatch works, so it's toggle-specific). I'll drive the menu with a colocated hook instead — sanctioned, deterministic, and I'll keep a plain `phx-click=\"nav-toggle\"` event so test clicks stay harmless.\n\n", [%{"arguments" => %{"new_string" => "        <.button\n          id={@toggle_id}\n          type=\"button\"\n          variant=\"ghost\"\n          shape=\"square\"\n          class=\"lg:hidden\"\n          aria-label=\"Toggle navigation menu\"\n          aria-controls={@menu_id}\n          phx-hook=\".AppNavToggle\"\n          phx-click=\"nav-toggle\"\n        >\n          <CoreComponents.icon name=\"hero-bars-3\" class=\"size-5\" />\n        </.button>\n      </div>\n\n      <div id={@menu_id} hidden phx-update=\"ignore\" class=\"basis-full\">", "old_string" => "        <.button\n          id={@toggle_id}\n          type=\"button\"\n          variant=\"ghost\"\n          shape=\"square\"\n          class=\"lg:hidden\"\n          aria-label=\"Toggle navigation menu\"\n          aria-controls={@menu_id}\n          phx-click={JS.toggle(to: \"#\#{@menu_id}\")}\n        >\n          <CoreComponents.icon name=\"hero-bars-3\" class=\"size-5\" />\n        </.button>\n      </div>\n\n      <div id={@menu_id} hidden class=\"basis-full\">", "path" => "benchapp/lib/benchapp_web/components/composite_components.ex"}, "id" => "chatcmpl-tool-9d0e6e37ef74cb69", "name" => "edit"}], "Confirmed: JS.toggle isn't functioning even on a fresh page with a single click. JS.dispatch works (theme). Something about the toggle operation is different — probably either the owner-view-based async execution queue is silently failing, or the theme toggle was working because the click handler for its dispatch ran at... something like that.\n\nWait, actually — did the theme toggle really work through the LV handler? The theme script is also listening for \"storage\" events! When you click the dark button: JS.dispatch(\"phx:set-theme\") dispatches an event on the button (e.target.dataset.phxTheme = \"dark\") → setTheme(\"dark\"). If dispatch didn't run, the theme shouldn't change... but it did change (the screenshot is dark). So dispatch did execute via the LV click handler.\n\nThe difference between the toggle and dispatch click handlers in LV 1.2: the handler collects all phx-* bindings on the element, executes them in order... for JS commands, it calls `execMany` on the view: `view.execJS`? The theme button and nav-toggle are both inside the same nav...\n\nHmm, one difference: the nav-toggle button in my app_nav has `type=\"button\"` and `aria-controls`... the theme button is type=\"button\". Both fine.\n\nAnother thought: does JS.toggle require `blocking` in the op queue and get dropped by my `phx-r=\"\"` static marker? Hmm.\n\nWhatever the root cause is — replace it with a colocated hook. Deterministic, and it's the sanctioned AGENTS approach for interop with client-side DOM.\n\nPlan:\n1. In app_nav: on the toggle button add `phx-hook=\".AppNavToggle\"` + `aria-controls={@menu_id}`; remove phx-click; append a colocated `<script :type={Phoenix.LiveView.ColocatedHook} name=\".AppNavToggle\">` at the end of the nav (inside the root of the component template — must be within the ~H template; AGENTS: it gets integrated into app.js automatically).\n\nWait — the colocated hook needs to be placed once per page; app_nav renders once per page. On /custom-designs with the preview, there are two app_nav instances → two hook attachments → both fine (each toggles its own aria-controls menu; preview uses different ids).\n\n2. Hook JS:\n```js\nexport default {\n  mounted() {\n    this.el.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n      const menu = document.getElementById(this.el.getAttribute(\"aria-controls\"));\n      if (menu) menu.toggleAttribute(\"hidden\");\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\nHmm — addEventListener on mount: even if the hook re-mounts due to morphing, listeners on this.el persist? If the element gets replaced by morph, mounted() re-runs on the new element. OK. Use a this.handleClick pattern with cleanup? LV hooks don't auto-remove listeners, but if el gets morphed, the old el gets GC'd. No problem.\n\nAlso, when clicking a link inside the menu, close the menu (nice UX: navigation happens anyway → on mobile a full page navigation via the navigate link? In LV, navigate link → live_redirect → the entire LV gets remounted → hook re-mounts → menu resets to hidden (since hidden is a static attribute, new DOM from the server? For live_redirect, new page renders → menu is hidden again. Good).\n\n3. Also, do I keep `phx-update=\"ignore\"`? The hook manages its own DOM (toggles the hidden attribute on #mobile-menu, which is inside the component's root, and could be morphed on re-render!). If a tick re-renders HomeLive, does #mobile-menu morph and lose its hidden attribute? #mobile-menu is inside Layouts.app which is rendered inside HomeLive.render — dynamic diff area: the layout component receives the same assigns (flash, active_nav, inner_content dynamic). LiveView diffs the static parts — app_nav is entirely static within the layout's compiled template (its attrs: id/active/brand/links — active changes per page but is static within a page; within a page's lifetime nothing changes) → server doesn't resend → morph doesn't touch it. But the flash_group's dynamic parts... are separate. So the menu stays open across ticks. AGENTS: \"if using phx-hook and that JS hook manages its own DOM, always also set phx-update='ignore'\" — the hook manages the menu's visibility; the hook is on the BUTTON, and " <> ..., ~U[2026-09-11 08:20:21.083657Z], "a2f6d7f0-8ae2-460a-98f7-31fa811e3d5d"]
